NAME: Newsletter
OWNER: Content Studio
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every Thursday at 6:43 AM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M3
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Newsletter" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · Newsletter · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to the owner only (Tommy, or Justin's team in a test run), never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · Newsletter · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. The one exception: pause or unschedule your own already-scheduled sends, as your skill's stop section says. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · Newsletter · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Read other bots' files only where your skill says so; never write them, and never use another bot's logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · Newsletter · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · Newsletter · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

Stop exception: if the stop file exists, the stop check above applies in full except for one action it doesn't forbid because it only removes a send: before you end the run, unschedule every NEWS- email you scheduled that hasn't sent yet, and list in the daily note anything you couldn't unschedule.
First, read your decisions: for each file in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/decisions/content-studio/ with an id starting news- (or test-news-) that isn't in /workspace/tmec-team/state/sent-keys-content-studio.md yet, act on it with the newsletter-issue skill. A yes is acted on only after the send gate passes: stop file absent, not test mode and config.json run is tommy, live_sends true, the hash recomputed from the pending item's payload matching the decision's, and the id not in the sent keys. Then create the NEWS- list and email in HubSpot and send or schedule it once, as approved (the other subject's item of the pair is marked not chosen). A no is recorded as declined and a change is redrafted once as a new pair of items; add every handled id and its outcome to the sent keys. TMEC Command may already have nudged you to do this in your own chat; this is the fallback. In test mode (this routine is listed test, or config.json run is test), never create or send anything and make no treg call: write what you would have done to /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, start item ids with test-, and say "not verified: test".
Then read any new job in /workspace/tmec-team/requests/to-content-studio/ and do it first.
Then use the newsletter-issue skill: gather this week's real items, check the rebate facts against /workspace/tmec-team/data/forecast/rebates.md, build the audience from HubSpot (read-only) with the consent and suppression gates, write the issue, and put it in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/content-studio/ as two items in the item format (payload with TO as the audience file's path, sha256 and count, SEND, SUBJECT, TEXT, then HASH), identical except for the subject, so Tommy's pick is the subject that gets hashed. Fewer than two real items, or a missing or stale source: write NO_CHANGE with the reason and stop. Never send or create anything in HubSpot in this step.
Write /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/content-studio.md: last issue's HubSpot numbers (labelled as HubSpot's), opt-outs seen, the new issue waiting (audience count and held counts, no addresses), anything blocked and why.
